WEBVTT

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.646
He's got temporal...
delirium.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.952
Trauma Team 4 to Level Red.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.288
Trauma Team 4
to Level Red.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.628
Reconnect to stations...

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.965
Code 4 Nursing Unit,
report to Level Red.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.800
He does have a sensor.
It's not working.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.476
Negative for dysplasia,
viremia, necrobiosis.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.307
Please extend your arms.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.837
Species: Dralian.
Identity: Gar.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.407
T.C. 15. You may proceed.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.488
Chellick.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.319
Lucky I caught you.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.825
Mr. Gar, I wish
I had time to talk.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.623
Well, all you have
to do is listen.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.754
I have a new supply
of cytogenics.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.765
Your last supply was useless.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.767
Expired lots, diluted samples.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.099
Oh, I have something
special this time.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.605
The latest in substandard
technology, no doubt.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.164
Oh, this item
is far from substandard.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.871
And as a gesture of goodwill,
I'm offering it to you first.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.346
We don't need
another neural monitor.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.883
Mm, this is much more
sophisticated than that.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.612
I'm sure it has
some ingenious use,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.119
but I'm not interested.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.784
Please state the nature...

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.454
of the medical emergency?

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.363
Where have you taken me?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.307
It's a holographic construct,
programmed with over

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.707
five million medical protocols.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.712
I demand to be returned
to Voyager at once.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.475
What's Voyager?

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.948
The Federation starship
to which I'm assigned.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.484
This man is a kidnapper.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.918
I would never offer you
stolen property.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.582
I traded warp-grade dilithium
for this program.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.783
What's your price?

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.257
This negotiation is pointless.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.919
I'm not about to perform
medical services

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.428
for a pair of common thieves.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.930
It doesn't seem
to be in working order.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.958
Trauma victims are now arriving
at Emergency Intake 7.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.867
What caused their injuries?

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.533
A generator explosion
at the Gammadan Mining Facility.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.373
You better start cooperating,
or I will dismantle your program

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.276
and sell it off
one subroutine at a time.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.645
When Captain Janeway
discovers what you've done...

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:10.808
Come on.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:11.872
Let's go, clear a path.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.509
We're gonna lose this guy.
Come on.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.450
Here we go.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.350
All right, tuck him in there.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.911
I can't find any coagulant.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.582
Somebody check the reserves.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:19.886
There are no reserves.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.790
Oh, this one's got
grade-4 pulmonary burns.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:25.763
Patient's T.C. Is 4.
Transfer to Level Green.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.823
Level Green isn't
equipped for this.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.130
His T.C.'s only 4.
Take him to Green.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.865
Don't touch that.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.271
This patient's bleeding
seriously.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.603
He needs an immediate infusion.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:37.938
What are you doing?

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.273
Get away from him.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.835
With technology this primitive,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.574
you may as well be using
leeches.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:43.946
Who is this man?

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.277
A doctor, of sorts.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.443
I thought you were

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.611
withholding your services.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.949
Fortunately for these patients,

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.683
I am programmed
with the Hippocratic oath.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.384
It requires me
to treat anyone who's ill.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:54.958
This patient needs
20 milligrams anesthezine.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:55.958
Get me a hypospray.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.562
A what?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.791
I'm sorry,
this may hurt a little.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.442
Did you have to program
that Nausicaan guard

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.884
to high stick so much?

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.079
Well, you play hockey,

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:23.884
you've got
to expect a few lumps.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.890
What are we gonna
tell the Doctor?

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.425
Hmm.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.791
You know how he feels
about our juvenile holoprograms.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:32.490
Relax.
I'll come up with something.

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.226
Hey, Doc.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.700
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.768
I know what you're thinking,

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.069
but there's
a simple explanation.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.574
Tell him, Tom.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.634
Right. Well, um, see, Doc,

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.510
we were running
these invasion scenarios

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.744
when this species
of proto-humanoid...

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.082
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.678
Are you okay, Doc?

00:05:56.756 --> 00:06:00.055
Please take an analgesic
and return in 24 hours.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.062
It's a replicated fake.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.893
The program running in Sick Bay

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.364
is from one of Doc's
old training files.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:12.302
I want someone to tell me
how this snake oil salesman

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:16.308
managed to evade every
security protocol on the ship.

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.708
I take full responsibility.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.109
I'm not interested in fault.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.874
I just want to know
how it happened.

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:24.644
Um, Gar spent the
night in Sick Bay.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:28.448
He claimed to have gotten
food poisoning at dinner.

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:29.920
He had plenty of time
to learn about

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.421
the mobile emitter
from the Doctor.

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:33.254
Who I'm sure was more
than willing to extol

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.418
its virtues.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:35.461
Medical logs show

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.291
the training file
was activated just before

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.297
Gar left Voyager.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:42.334
Scan for his ion trail,
and let's review safeguards

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:45.735
for accessing low-security
files, shall we, Mr. Tuvok?

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.071
Captain, don't blame
Tuvok for what happened.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:51.405
It was my fault.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.910
How so?

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:56.847
Gar kept complaining
how bland his dinner was,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.851
so I added a few exotic spices.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.511
I'm not sure I see your point.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.283
I-I was trying so hard to
create something he liked

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:07.258
that I didn't take his alien
physiology into account.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:09.521
Everyone's assuming
he faked his illness,

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.688
but I might have
really made him sick.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:15.359
It's not as if your cooking
turned him into a thief.

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:17.562
No, but if he hadn't
gone to Sick Bay,

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:19.730
he may never have
come up with a plan

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:21.000
to kidnap the Doctor,

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.371
much less have
the opportunity to do it.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.808
In my experience, Neelix,

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:27.641
men like Gar have no trouble
finding opportunities

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.544
to take advantage
of other people.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.049
Well, I just hope there's
something I can do

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.710
to help find the Doctor.

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:36.186
Well, when and if
that opportunity arises,

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:38.416
I'm sure you'll make
the most of it.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.733
That was the most impressive
cortical bypass I've ever seen.

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.899
It's just a question
of possessing the basic skills.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.374
Ah, if I had
basic skills like yours,

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:58.876
they'd move me up to Level Blue.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.173
Take this patient to Yellow.

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.941
You seem a little low
on resources here.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.504
If I could contact
my medical staff,

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.847
I might be able to get you
some additional supplies.

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.351
Uh, communication is
usually restricted,

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.251
but the Allocator
might give you clearance.

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.085
Good. Where can I find him?

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:12.886
Uh, the Allocator isn't a him.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.424
It's our main computer.

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.325
Well...

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:18.454
Perhaps it could establish
a communications link

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.691
with Voyager's main computer.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.265
You'll have to submit
a formal request to Chellick

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:25.361
and support it
with Form 83-W in triplicate.

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:26.530
Even then...

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.708
Why hasn't this patient
been treated yet?

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.505
He's waiting for proton imaging.

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:35.012
There are a lot of other people
ahead of him.

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:38.050
It's nice to see someone
knows what's going on.

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:39.550
What's your name?

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:41.052
Tebbis.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.917
Well, Tebbis,
this doesn't look too serious.

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:45.889
Uh, it's just a little
osteal extravasation.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:48.222
Excellent diagnosis.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:50.194
I hope to be a doctor someday.

00:08:50.263 --> 00:08:52.322
Really? Well, I hope
your working conditions

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:53.763
are better than these.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:54.765
It wouldn't be so bad

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.233
if they'd let us listen
to music.

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:57.929
It would certainly
improve my mood.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.266
It's not just that,

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.568
but music has
great healing power.

00:09:01.641 --> 00:09:03.836
I couldn't agree
with you more.

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:08.176
Uh, exhale slowly.

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.340
Can't you give him
a neural blocker?

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:12.281
He's already had his allocation.

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:19.156
The leg injury isn't all
I'm picking up.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.193
He's got some kind
of systemic disease.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.421
It's a chromo-viral infection.

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:25.862
We have 12 cases down here.

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:27.524
He's in the final stage.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.534
Is there an
established treatment?

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.593
Cytoglobin injections.

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:34.769
These scans don't show
any cytoglobin

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.898
in his bloodstream.

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:37.600
He hasn't been given any.

00:09:37.677 --> 00:09:38.735
Why not?

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:40.642
He doesn't have
a high enough T.C.

00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:41.805
"T.C."? What's that?

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:43.178
Ah, there you are.

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.443
I'm happy to report

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.610
that I've acquired your program
from Gar.

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:47.914
Please come with me.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.282
I will not.

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:50.447
May I remind you

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:51.922
I'm being illegally detained?

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:54.619
Or hasn't the rule of law
reached this society yet?

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:58.027
We follow the Allocator's rules,
and it's determined

00:09:58.097 --> 00:10:01.032
that your services are
required on Level Blue.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.694
Eh, please, Doctor,
the Allocator knows

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:06.329
which patients
need help the most.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:17.577
Level Blue is your critical care
area, I presume.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.915
Level Blue is the area
where it's most critical

00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:23.353
that we provide excellent care.

00:10:35.668 --> 00:10:38.694
These patients will be
your chief responsibility

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:40.204
from now on.

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:42.706
Do whatever you can
to make them well.

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:52.977
Why are these patients
getting preferential treatment?

00:10:53.119 --> 00:10:55.212
They have a higher T.C.
Than the others.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:58.154
Indulge me.
What's T. C?

00:10:58.224 --> 00:10:59.452
Treatment Coefficient.

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:01.652
The Allocator assigns one
to every patient.

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:04.355
It determines the level
of care they receive.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.127
How is this
coefficient derived?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.633
Through a complex formula

00:11:09.702 --> 00:11:12.227
that involves profession,
skills, accomplishments...

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:15.239
How is any of that relevant
to medical treatment?

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:16.740
An agricultural engineer

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:19.403
is obviously more important
than a waste processor.

00:11:19.478 --> 00:11:21.070
Important to whom?

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:22.375
Society.

00:11:22.448 --> 00:11:24.882
When your resources are limited,

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.383
you have to prioritize.

00:11:26.452 --> 00:11:27.749
So you base treatment

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.948
on whether patients have
particular abilities?

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:33.355
It's much more
complicated than that.

00:11:33.426 --> 00:11:37.487
The Allocator assesses
the entire individual.

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.929
And reduces his life
to a number.

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:41.489
It may seem impersonal,
but it's what

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:43.159
the Dinaali
have contracted us to do.

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:45.260
Chellick's people are known
throughout the sector

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:46.964
for their
administrative skills.

00:11:47.073 --> 00:11:50.099
Before they came here,
we were a dying race.

00:11:50.176 --> 00:11:52.076
Eco-disasters, famine...

00:11:52.144 --> 00:11:53.907
Dr. Dysek, Chief of Medicine.

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.777
The medical hologram
I told you about.

00:11:56.849 --> 00:11:58.544
Are you in charge
of what passes for care

00:11:58.617 --> 00:11:59.982
on Level Red?

00:12:00.086 --> 00:12:02.486
Because those people
are suffering.

00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:04.648
Intriguing technology.

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:07.420
Can we use him
to treat patients yet?

00:12:07.493 --> 00:12:08.926
That's what he's here for.

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:11.360
In some societies,
it's considered rude

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.057
to refer to someone
in the third person

00:12:13.132 --> 00:12:15.498
while he's standing
in front of you.

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:17.502
I'm sure
you'll make good use of him.

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:28.811
The warp trail ends here.

00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:30.314
Gar should be directly ahead.

00:12:30.382 --> 00:12:31.406
All stop.

00:12:31.484 --> 00:12:33.418
Red Alert.

00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:35.477
On screen.

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:39.856
It's emitting
a false warp signature.

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:43.622
Looks like we've underestimated
Mr. Gar again.

00:12:43.696 --> 00:12:44.958
Now what?

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.691
There may be another way
to find him.

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.961
What do you have in mind?

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.695
He traded us high-grade iridium,

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.863
which has
a very brief half-life.

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:54.803
His ship is slow.

00:12:54.874 --> 00:12:57.172
Logic suggests
he acquired the substance

00:12:57.243 --> 00:12:58.972
within a radius
of three light-years.

00:12:59.111 --> 00:13:01.807
Cross-reference our sensor logs
and long-range scans.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:07.378
Two planets,
no atmosphere or technology

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:09.546
a T-class nebula...

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:10.748
Here's something.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:13.883
An asteroid with approximately
200 humanoid life signs,

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.189
subterranean structures.

00:13:16.262 --> 00:13:17.889
Sounds like a mining operation.

00:13:17.963 --> 00:13:19.760
If that's where Mr. Gar acquired

00:13:19.832 --> 00:13:22.426
the iridium, they may be able
to help us find him.

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:25.493
Tom, how fast
can you get us there?

00:13:25.571 --> 00:13:26.868
Less than two hours.

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:28.270
Do it.

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:35.037
We're being hailed.

00:13:35.114 --> 00:13:36.376
Open a channel.

00:13:37.783 --> 00:13:40.445
I want my iridium back now.

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:42.077
I beg your pardon?

00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:43.382
I've scanned your ship.

00:13:43.455 --> 00:13:44.854
I know you've got it on board.

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:48.291
Yes, we obtained it from a man
called Gar, a merchant...

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.418
You mean thief.

00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:52.726
So, you have
had the pleasure of meeting him.

00:13:52.798 --> 00:13:53.890
He was here two days ago.

00:13:53.966 --> 00:13:56.230
He sold us
3,000 induction units.

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:57.929
He was gone a day
before we realized

00:13:58.003 --> 00:14:00.369
he'd also stolen 20 kilos
of ore.

00:14:00.439 --> 00:14:03.738
We had a similar experience.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:05.777
Maybe we can help each other.

00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:07.574
How?

00:14:07.646 --> 00:14:10.274
Do you have any idea
where we might find him?

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:12.715
Will you return my iridium?

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:14.047
By all means,

00:14:14.119 --> 00:14:16.781
but Gar only traded us half
of what he stole from you.

00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:19.916
However, we might be able
to get the rest of it back.

00:14:19.992 --> 00:14:22.654
All I can tell you is
that the induction units

00:14:22.728 --> 00:14:24.958
came from a planetoid
called Velos.

00:14:29.201 --> 00:14:31.533
You may go.

00:14:31.604 --> 00:14:33.663
Your surgical technique
is impressive.

00:14:33.739 --> 00:14:35.206
Well, you've obviously
had experience

00:14:35.274 --> 00:14:36.605
with cellular repair.

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:37.642
As a matter of fact,

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.575
I've done extensive
research on the subject.

00:14:39.645 --> 00:14:41.545
I'd be happy
to share it with you,

00:14:41.614 --> 00:14:44.105
but we'll have to contact
Voyager to get it.

00:14:44.183 --> 00:14:46.151
You'll have to discuss that
with Chellick.

00:14:46.218 --> 00:14:48.186
He authorizes
all communications.

00:14:49.889 --> 00:14:51.948
It's time for this patient's
next injection.

00:14:52.057 --> 00:14:54.184
Requesting one
cytoglobin injection

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.093
for patient B-3,
priority Blue-7 gamma.

00:14:57.162 --> 00:14:59.926
One cytoglobin injection
authorized.

00:15:03.335 --> 00:15:06.896
Does this patient have
a chromo-viral infection?

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:08.166
No. Why?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.537
I was told

00:15:09.608 --> 00:15:12.042
cytoglobin is the standard
treatment for that disease.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:15.808
Cytoglobin also prevents
arterial aging.

00:15:15.881 --> 00:15:18.714
Will that be all?

00:15:18.784 --> 00:15:20.775
You may go.

00:15:20.853 --> 00:15:22.821
This patient's arteries
appear to be healthy.

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:25.584
At the moment,
but daily injections

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:28.422
increase life expectancy
up to 40 percent.

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:30.758
We prescribe them
for all Level Blue patients.

00:15:30.829 --> 00:15:34.128
I just saw a boy
on Level Red who's dying.

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:36.360
This medicine
could save his life.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:39.097
This woman is a Chief Engineer
of an irrigation facility

00:15:39.171 --> 00:15:41.571
which provides water
to half the subcontinent.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.471
So her life is more valuable?

00:15:43.542 --> 00:15:46.272
Keeping her healthy
contributes to our survival.

00:15:46.345 --> 00:15:48.540
Can you say the same
for the boy on Level Red?

00:15:48.614 --> 00:15:50.844
Who knows what he'll accomplish
if he has the chance.

00:15:50.916 --> 00:15:53.851
If he becomes more valuable
to society, his T.C. Will rise,

00:15:53.919 --> 00:15:55.944
and then he'll receive
better treatment.

00:15:56.088 --> 00:15:57.680
He may not be around
long enough.

00:15:57.756 --> 00:15:59.121
I'm sorry he's sick,

00:15:59.191 --> 00:16:01.125
but our society
is much better off

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:05.220
since we began following
the Allocator's protocols.

00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:09.998
Some of you are.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:17.839
I never expected
to see you again.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.842
Why do you say that?

00:16:18.911 --> 00:16:20.845
Level Blue is much
more prestigious.

00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:23.347
Prestige is the least
of my concerns.

00:16:23.415 --> 00:16:24.848
How is he?

00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:26.179
Not well.

00:16:31.457 --> 00:16:33.925
His condition's
deteriorated so rapidly.

00:16:34.026 --> 00:16:36.722
His coenzyme allotment's
been reduced.

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:38.729
Are we here to help
these people or kill them?

00:16:38.797 --> 00:16:41.595
His T.C. Is just too low.

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:42.929
Maybe we can raise it.

00:16:43.068 --> 00:16:44.365
That's not possible.

00:16:44.436 --> 00:16:46.165
If it's purely
a function of statistics,

00:16:46.238 --> 00:16:48.035
we can simply input more data.

00:16:48.107 --> 00:16:49.404
We're not
authorized to do th...

00:16:49.475 --> 00:16:50.601
Voje.

00:16:50.676 --> 00:16:52.644
When you look
at your patient lying there,

00:16:52.711 --> 00:16:55.441
you have to ask yourself:
What can I do?

00:16:55.514 --> 00:16:57.243
What must I do?

00:16:57.316 --> 00:17:00.444
We can amend his database
to include

00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:01.713
additional skills.

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:02.776
Such as?

00:17:02.855 --> 00:17:05.585
His extensive knowledge
of neutronics.

00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:07.454
He doesn't know anything
about neutronics.

00:17:07.526 --> 00:17:09.221
We can say he does.

00:17:09.294 --> 00:17:11.057
What's the harm in trying?

00:17:15.501 --> 00:17:17.662
Amend patient R-12's T.C.

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:20.899
To include an expertise
in neutronics.

00:17:20.973 --> 00:17:22.838
Unable to verify.

00:17:22.908 --> 00:17:24.307
Amendment denied.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.071
You see?

00:17:26.145 --> 00:17:27.544
Hello.

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:28.705
Lie still.

00:17:28.781 --> 00:17:30.840
What are you doing?

00:17:30.916 --> 00:17:33.350
Trying to get you
the proper medication.

00:17:33.419 --> 00:17:36.616
You're wasting time

00:17:36.688 --> 00:17:38.918
you could be spending
with other patients.

00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:41.390
You have as much right
to treatment as anyone.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.827
It's not your fault.

00:17:46.865 --> 00:17:48.958
There's nothing you can do.

00:18:00.446 --> 00:18:01.504
Nurse.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.547
Yes, Doctor?

00:18:02.614 --> 00:18:04.081
Why hasn't this patient received

00:18:04.149 --> 00:18:06.049
her additional
cytoglobin injection?

00:18:06.118 --> 00:18:07.176
Additional?

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:08.378
If you'd examine her chart,

00:18:08.454 --> 00:18:10.115
you'd see that I've
increased her dosage.

00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:11.884
Dr. Dysek didn't say anything...

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.548
Dr. Dysek is at home
with his family.

00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:15.593
Would you like me to contact him
so you can explain

00:18:15.661 --> 00:18:16.821
why you're not doing your job?

00:18:16.895 --> 00:18:20.023
No, Doctor.

00:18:20.099 --> 00:18:22.863
Requesting
one cytoglobin injection

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:26.871
for patient B-3,
priority Blue-7 gamma.

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:29.669
One cytoglobin injection
authorized.

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.173
I'll do it myself.

00:18:36.248 --> 00:18:37.840
Can I assist you?

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:41.408
You may go.

00:19:35.774 --> 00:19:37.867
He convinced me to let him
take the induction units

00:19:37.943 --> 00:19:38.910
on consignment.

00:19:39.044 --> 00:19:40.909
That was more than ten days ago.

00:19:40.979 --> 00:19:42.776
I haven't heard from him since.

00:19:42.848 --> 00:19:45.908
You appear to be an experienced
merchant, Mr. Kipp.

00:19:46.018 --> 00:19:48.213
Why would you trust
someone like Gar?

00:19:48.287 --> 00:19:50.414
He came highly recommended.

00:19:50.489 --> 00:19:51.547
By whom?

00:19:51.623 --> 00:19:52.715
A buyer I know.

00:19:52.791 --> 00:19:54.019
He said he's been trading

00:19:54.092 --> 00:19:55.787
with Gar for years.

00:19:55.861 --> 00:19:58.591
Do you know where we
can find this buyer?

00:19:58.664 --> 00:20:00.131
Yes, Captain.

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:02.861
I am the fool who said
that Gar could be trusted.

00:20:02.935 --> 00:20:05.403
Sounds like you've
changed your mind.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.769
I should have known
it was a mistake, but...

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:13.539
Well... you see, I have never
been able to say no to my wife.

00:20:13.612 --> 00:20:15.512
What does she have
to do with it?

00:20:15.581 --> 00:20:18.641
Well, she's the one who asked me
to recommend Gar.

00:20:18.717 --> 00:20:20.412
Then she must know him well.

00:20:20.485 --> 00:20:24.080
They're... friends.

00:20:24.156 --> 00:20:26.181
May we speak with her?

00:20:26.258 --> 00:20:28.453
She's, uh...

00:20:28.527 --> 00:20:30.461
Well, she's not here.

00:20:30.529 --> 00:20:33.123
Do you know
where we might find her?

00:20:33.198 --> 00:20:36.463
She left me.

00:20:39.104 --> 00:20:40.264
You're a woman.

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:41.931
You saw my husband
with your own eyes...

00:20:42.007 --> 00:20:43.599
overweight, depressed.

00:20:43.675 --> 00:20:45.472
You would have left him, too,

00:20:45.544 --> 00:20:49.446
especially if you had met
someone as exciting as Gar.

00:20:49.514 --> 00:20:51.482
Yes, he's very exciting.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.348
That's why you're looking
for him, isn't it?

00:20:54.419 --> 00:20:56.080
You want him for yourself.

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:59.453
I assure you, I have no romantic
interest in him whatsoever.

00:20:59.524 --> 00:21:01.958
Why? Not good enough for you?

00:21:02.027 --> 00:21:03.119
No, it's not that.

00:21:03.195 --> 00:21:05.163
It's just that...

00:21:07.199 --> 00:21:10.100
I already have a man.

00:21:12.571 --> 00:21:15.699
We have a business opportunity
for Mr. Gar...

00:21:15.774 --> 00:21:19.141
one that will expire
if we don't find him soon.

00:21:19.211 --> 00:21:22.612
He's on his way
to the gambling tournament

00:21:22.681 --> 00:21:23.773
on Selek IV.

00:21:23.849 --> 00:21:27.444
When you see him,
tell him to hurry home.

00:21:46.738 --> 00:21:48.706
How are you feeling?

00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:51.542
Better.

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:52.702
That's what happens

00:21:52.778 --> 00:21:54.405
when you get
the proper treatment.

00:21:57.582 --> 00:22:00.710
But I'm not authorized
to receive cytoglobin.

00:22:00.786 --> 00:22:01.878
You are now.

00:22:01.953 --> 00:22:03.818
You'll need
several more injections,

00:22:03.889 --> 00:22:05.914
but you can expect
a complete recovery.

00:22:06.058 --> 00:22:08.652
Whatever you did,
they'll find out.

00:22:08.727 --> 00:22:09.921
They'll punish you.

00:22:10.062 --> 00:22:12.223
You're assuming
I've done something illicit.

00:22:12.297 --> 00:22:13.229
Didn't you?

00:22:13.298 --> 00:22:14.390
Of course not.

00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:16.093
I simply had a talk
with Chellick,

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:18.602
explained to him
what a bright young man you are,

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.036
and he had the Allocator
recalculate your T.C.

00:22:21.106 --> 00:22:23.939
I've never met
a doctor like you.

00:22:24.076 --> 00:22:25.703
Well... it's not hard
to stand out

00:22:25.777 --> 00:22:28.109
when the general level
of competence is so low.

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.545
There are patients

00:22:29.614 --> 00:22:32.447
on this level who deserve
a higher T.C. Than I do.

00:22:32.517 --> 00:22:34.712
Could you talk to Chellick
about them?

00:22:43.128 --> 00:22:44.686
Thank you.

00:22:51.169 --> 00:22:52.431
Ah, Voje.

00:22:52.504 --> 00:22:53.596
You're not busy, are you?

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:55.264
Well, actually, I was just...

00:22:55.340 --> 00:22:57.433
Good. I want you to help me
dispense these injections.

00:22:57.509 --> 00:22:58.771
Where did you get
the cytoglobin?

00:22:58.844 --> 00:22:59.776
Level Blue. Where else?

00:22:59.845 --> 00:23:00.971
You stole it?

00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:02.911
I'd prefer to think of it
as "reallocation."

00:23:03.014 --> 00:23:04.140
We're going to treat every

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:05.706
chromo-virus patient
on this level.

00:23:05.784 --> 00:23:06.751
Do you have any idea

00:23:06.818 --> 00:23:08.752
what kind of trouble
we could get into?

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:10.549
"We?" Then you will help me.

00:23:10.622 --> 00:23:12.385
Uh, no! Absolutely not!

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:15.187
Modifying data files
was bad enough.

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:17.558
Well, I certainly wouldn't
want you to do anything

00:23:17.629 --> 00:23:18.857
to compromise your ethics.

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:20.557
I'll help you.

00:23:22.033 --> 00:23:23.466
You should be in bed.

00:23:23.535 --> 00:23:24.934
Actually, now that
he's improving,

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:26.628
a little activity
will do him good.

00:23:26.705 --> 00:23:30.505
You can go back to doing...
whatever you were doing.

00:23:37.048 --> 00:23:40.142
The best place
to inject him is here

00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:42.846
in the lateral artery.

00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:47.820
Excellent work.

00:23:47.893 --> 00:23:50.225
It's nice to see
someone in this hospital

00:23:50.295 --> 00:23:51.762
has a future as a healer.

00:23:53.031 --> 00:23:54.965
If we each take a third
of the patients,

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:57.466
maybe we can finish
before someone catches us.

00:24:03.675 --> 00:24:05.233
Who do you think you are,

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:08.746
prescribing unnecessary
medications for my patients?

00:24:08.814 --> 00:24:10.281
It wasn't unnecessary.

00:24:10.348 --> 00:24:12.873
If you believe that,
you're incompetent,

00:24:12.951 --> 00:24:14.612
or perhaps malfunctioning.

00:24:14.686 --> 00:24:19.453
I was simply trying to increase
our allocation of resources.

00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:21.788
What are you talking about?

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:23.122
I did some checking.

00:24:23.195 --> 00:24:26.460
Last month, Level Blue's
total medication requests

00:24:26.531 --> 00:24:27.793
were down by 6 percent.

00:24:27.866 --> 00:24:29.458
Because our cure rate
was higher.

00:24:29.534 --> 00:24:30.831
Exactly.

00:24:30.902 --> 00:24:33.234
Because you performed
so efficiently last month,

00:24:33.305 --> 00:24:36.172
the Allocator will determine
you're able to do with less

00:24:36.241 --> 00:24:37.833
next month.

00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:40.139
If we don't order
more medication now,

00:24:40.212 --> 00:24:43.670
we may not get it...
when we need it.

00:24:43.748 --> 00:24:45.238
Think about it, Doctor.

00:24:45.317 --> 00:24:47.808
If you don't have
the proper resources,

00:24:47.886 --> 00:24:50.354
your cure rate could go down.

00:24:50.422 --> 00:24:51.787
If that happens...

00:24:51.857 --> 00:24:54.348
the Allocator may assign you
to a lower level.

00:24:54.426 --> 00:24:55.518
Mm-hmm.

00:24:55.594 --> 00:24:57.528
Are we having a problem

00:24:57.596 --> 00:24:59.826
with our newest piece
of technology?

00:24:59.898 --> 00:25:01.866
Actually...

00:25:03.134 --> 00:25:05.432
...he seems to be
learning the system...

00:25:05.504 --> 00:25:07.563
quite well.

00:25:16.848 --> 00:25:18.213
Oh. Three of the patients
we injected

00:25:18.283 --> 00:25:19.443
are practically virus-free.

00:25:19.518 --> 00:25:22.282
What did you expect?

00:25:22.354 --> 00:25:26.256
Um, maybe we could "reallocate"
other medications,

00:25:26.324 --> 00:25:27.586
treat more patients.

00:25:27.659 --> 00:25:28.785
Now you're thinking
like a doctor.

00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:30.122
And to support your efforts,

00:25:30.195 --> 00:25:32.425
I've arranged
for resources from Level Blue

00:25:32.497 --> 00:25:34.931
to be diverted here
on a regular basis.

00:25:35.033 --> 00:25:36.261
How did you manage that?

00:25:36.334 --> 00:25:37.426
Let's just say,

00:25:37.502 --> 00:25:40.630
Dr. Dysek and I have developed
a professional rapport.

00:25:40.705 --> 00:25:42.673
Sometimes I even
surprise myself.

00:25:44.543 --> 00:25:47.103
We may actually
make these people better.

00:25:47.178 --> 00:25:50.306
That feeling you get
from healing someone...

00:25:50.382 --> 00:25:52.282
infectious, isn't it?

00:25:56.021 --> 00:25:57.613
Where did you get that?

00:25:57.689 --> 00:25:59.884
One of the technicians
was going to recycle it

00:25:59.958 --> 00:26:02.426
because it wasn't working,
but I think I fixed it.

00:26:04.829 --> 00:26:08.094
Seems to be in good condition.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:09.258
And so do you.

00:26:09.334 --> 00:26:11.063
You'll be well enough
to leave soon.

00:26:11.136 --> 00:26:14.503
Couldn't you say I'm still sick?

00:26:14.573 --> 00:26:16.234
Don't you want to go home?

00:26:16.308 --> 00:26:17.639
If I do,

00:26:17.709 --> 00:26:20.041
they'll send me to work
in the refinery with my father.

00:26:20.111 --> 00:26:22.579
What about school?
Your medical training?

00:26:22.647 --> 00:26:25.411
I would never be authorized
for that.

00:26:25.483 --> 00:26:27.075
He's right.

00:26:27.152 --> 00:26:29.518
If I stay here,
you can teach me,

00:26:29.588 --> 00:26:31.852
and I can help you
treat your patients.

00:26:34.125 --> 00:26:37.094
I'm not planning
on being here that long myself.

00:26:38.797 --> 00:26:41.163
Then I can help Dr. Voje.

00:26:45.637 --> 00:26:47.662
We'll see what we can do.

00:26:52.711 --> 00:26:54.941
I have picked up Gar's ship,
directly ahead.

00:26:55.046 --> 00:26:56.809
Again?

00:26:56.881 --> 00:26:58.348
I'm reading his bio-signs.

00:26:58.416 --> 00:27:00.941
Any sign of the Doctor
or his emitter?

00:27:01.086 --> 00:27:02.110
Not yet.

00:27:02.187 --> 00:27:03.779
Should I hail Gar?

00:27:03.855 --> 00:27:06.346
If we let him know we're here,
he may try to slip away.

00:27:06.424 --> 00:27:08.187
We could drop out of warp
at close range

00:27:08.259 --> 00:27:10.352
and grab him before he knows
what's happening.

00:27:10.428 --> 00:27:11.690
I like it.

00:27:11.763 --> 00:27:13.526
Tom...

00:27:13.598 --> 00:27:16.158
Tuvok.

00:27:21.239 --> 00:27:22.831
He's hailing.

00:27:22.907 --> 00:27:25.034
I guess we put him
in the mood to talk.

00:27:25.110 --> 00:27:27.340
On screen.

00:27:27.412 --> 00:27:29.073
I thought we were friends,
Captain.

00:27:29.147 --> 00:27:30.705
Why am I being treated this way?

00:27:30.782 --> 00:27:32.409
I think I deserve better.

00:27:32.484 --> 00:27:34.076
Where's our Doctor?

00:27:34.152 --> 00:27:35.312
I have no idea.

00:27:35.387 --> 00:27:37.787
I certainly hope
nothing's happened to him.

00:27:37.856 --> 00:27:39.153
Scans are complete.

00:27:39.224 --> 00:27:40.418
Neither the mobile emitter

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:42.119
nor the Doctor's program
are aboard

00:27:42.193 --> 00:27:43.660
Gar's ship.

00:27:43.728 --> 00:27:46.356
Well, of course they're not.

00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:51.495
He's trying
to destabilize the tractor beam

00:27:51.569 --> 00:27:52.695
with a feedback pulse.

00:27:52.771 --> 00:27:54.739
Compensating.

00:27:54.806 --> 00:27:57.104
Don't bother, Harry.

00:27:58.476 --> 00:28:01.001
Just beam him to the brig.

00:28:11.322 --> 00:28:15.759
Tebbis... wake up.

00:28:15.827 --> 00:28:17.954
Time to make our rounds.

00:28:20.665 --> 00:28:22.895
Locate patient R-12.

00:28:23.001 --> 00:28:26.801
Patient R-12 has been
transferred to Level White.

00:28:28.339 --> 00:28:29.601
Tebbis has been moved.

00:28:29.674 --> 00:28:30.766
I know.

00:28:30.842 --> 00:28:31.900
What's Level White?

00:28:32.010 --> 00:28:33.739
Some kind of patient
recovery area?

00:28:33.812 --> 00:28:36.007
It's the morgue.

00:28:48.093 --> 00:28:50.459
I demand an explanation
for the death of that boy.

00:28:52.464 --> 00:28:54.489
I'm responsible
for thousands of patients.

00:28:54.566 --> 00:28:56.158
You'll have to be more specific.

00:28:56.234 --> 00:28:58.361
His name was Tebbis.

00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:01.433
Patient R-12.

00:29:03.908 --> 00:29:07.002
Acute chromo-viral disease.

00:29:07.078 --> 00:29:08.841
He was recovering.

00:29:08.913 --> 00:29:10.676
Apparently,
he developed complications.

00:29:10.749 --> 00:29:12.376
What kind of complications?

00:29:12.450 --> 00:29:13.974
A secondary infection.

00:29:14.052 --> 00:29:15.314
It spread rapidly.

00:29:15.386 --> 00:29:16.751
How was it treated?

00:29:16.821 --> 00:29:17.845
It wasn't.

00:29:17.922 --> 00:29:20.823
The patient had exceeded
his medication allotment.

00:29:20.892 --> 00:29:23.827
It seems someone had given him
unauthorized injections.

00:29:25.797 --> 00:29:28.322
Did you think
I wouldn't find out?

00:29:33.738 --> 00:29:36.832
Don't you have
any ethical standards?

00:29:36.908 --> 00:29:39.741
You are hardly in a position
to speak to me of ethics.

00:29:39.811 --> 00:29:41.176
Lying, stealing...

00:29:41.246 --> 00:29:43.271
Any other crimes
you wish to confess?

00:29:43.348 --> 00:29:45.407
I was trying to save lives.

00:29:45.483 --> 00:29:47.383
And I am trying
to save a society.

00:29:47.452 --> 00:29:51.081
Do you really think patient R-12
is going to help me do that?!

00:29:51.156 --> 00:29:53.215
His name was Tebbis.

00:29:53.291 --> 00:29:54.451
He wasn't contributing.

00:29:54.526 --> 00:29:56.016
He was a drain on resources.

00:29:56.094 --> 00:29:57.755
You're not just rationing
health care here.

00:29:57.829 --> 00:29:59.524
You're getting rid of the sick
and the weak.

00:29:59.597 --> 00:30:02.088
If the boy had been fit,
he would have survived.

00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:03.998
Why don't you just put a phaser
to their heads?

00:30:05.436 --> 00:30:07.063
We're healers, not killers.

00:30:09.174 --> 00:30:10.801
I'm going to expose you.

00:30:10.875 --> 00:30:13.105
To whom...
the people who employ me?

00:30:13.178 --> 00:30:16.306
They brought me here
to make the hard choices

00:30:16.381 --> 00:30:17.746
they don't want to make.

00:30:17.816 --> 00:30:20.580
From now on, I'm restricting you
to Level Blue.

00:30:20.652 --> 00:30:23.621
You've done enough damage
on Red.

00:30:23.688 --> 00:30:25.849
You mean those patients
that I treated?

00:30:25.924 --> 00:30:27.858
Yes, that was inconsiderate
of me.

00:30:27.926 --> 00:30:29.757
It was. You managed
to exceed their annual

00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:31.625
medication allotment
in a matter of days.

00:30:31.696 --> 00:30:32.788
They're being sent home.

00:30:32.864 --> 00:30:34.957
They'll die.

00:30:35.033 --> 00:30:36.261
You should have considered

00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:37.926
the consequences
of your actions.

00:30:38.002 --> 00:30:42.166
Please, don't make them suffer
for my mistakes.

00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:44.231
It won't happen again.

00:30:44.309 --> 00:30:45.799
I'm making certain of that.

00:30:45.877 --> 00:30:48.675
From now on, your time
will be strictly regulated.

00:30:48.746 --> 00:30:50.077
Meaning what?

00:30:50.148 --> 00:30:52.878
I've interfaced your holo-matrix
with the Allocator.

00:30:52.951 --> 00:30:55.977
Starting now, it will determine
where you go, when you go,

00:30:56.087 --> 00:30:57.952
and what you do
when you get there.

00:30:58.022 --> 00:30:59.853
The Medical Hologram

00:30:59.924 --> 00:31:02.119
will now commence treatment
on Level Blue.

00:31:04.863 --> 00:31:08.697
You have six minutes
to treat patient B-3.

00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:17.537
I don't know where he is.

00:31:17.609 --> 00:31:21.204
Not now, perhaps, but you know
where you took him.

00:31:21.279 --> 00:31:24.737
The last time I saw him,
he was in your Sick Bay.

00:31:24.816 --> 00:31:26.875
If you refuse to cooperate,

00:31:26.951 --> 00:31:30.751
your knowledge of his location
can be extracted.

00:31:30.822 --> 00:31:32.585
How?

00:31:32.657 --> 00:31:34.682
A mind-meld.

00:31:34.759 --> 00:31:37.523
W-what's that?

00:31:37.595 --> 00:31:39.586
An invasive
and disturbing procedure.

00:31:40.665 --> 00:31:41.654
Dinnertime!

00:31:41.733 --> 00:31:42.961
Mr. Neelix,

00:31:43.067 --> 00:31:45.831
I am in the middle
of an interrogation.

00:31:45.904 --> 00:31:48.600
Commander, you know
better than anyone

00:31:48.673 --> 00:31:51.233
that Starfleet
has strict guidelines

00:31:51.309 --> 00:31:53.573
about allowing prisoners to eat.

00:31:53.645 --> 00:31:54.737
Very well.

00:31:54.812 --> 00:31:56.006
I'll wait.

00:31:58.917 --> 00:32:01.283
There we are.

00:32:04.022 --> 00:32:06.047
I'm glad to see you
enjoying a meal.

00:32:06.124 --> 00:32:08.786
When you got sick last time,
I thought my food

00:32:08.860 --> 00:32:10.760
was to blame, until I realized

00:32:10.828 --> 00:32:15.788
it was just a ruse for you
to get close to the Doctor.

00:32:15.867 --> 00:32:19.234
I used Talaxian wormroot
as the base.

00:32:19.304 --> 00:32:20.896
Mm-hmm.

00:32:20.972 --> 00:32:22.064
I'm glad you like it.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:23.471
Some people react badly.

00:32:26.144 --> 00:32:27.736
React how?

00:32:27.812 --> 00:32:30.076
Oh, dear, I hope
you're not getting sick.

00:32:30.148 --> 00:32:31.581
Mm.

00:32:31.649 --> 00:32:34.812
If it's the wormroot,
it's gonna get a lot worse.

00:32:34.886 --> 00:32:37.116
What have you done to me?

00:32:37.188 --> 00:32:39.952
The usual symptoms
are abdominal spasms,

00:32:40.091 --> 00:32:42.059
which increase in severity

00:32:42.126 --> 00:32:44.560
for 30 hours...

00:32:44.629 --> 00:32:46.290
40 at the most.

00:32:46.364 --> 00:32:47.490
Tuvok to Sick Bay.

00:32:47.565 --> 00:32:48.759
Don't worry, Mr. Tuvok,

00:32:48.833 --> 00:32:50.095
it's not fatal.

00:32:50.168 --> 00:32:52.295
It's horribly unpleasant,
but, uh...

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:53.598
there's an antidote.

00:32:53.671 --> 00:32:55.366
Then give it to me!

00:32:55.440 --> 00:32:57.374
Unfortunately,

00:32:57.442 --> 00:33:01.469
our Doctor is the only one
authorized to administer it.

00:33:01.546 --> 00:33:04.413
Maybe if you remembered
where he was...

00:33:06.718 --> 00:33:08.583
Mr. Neelix...

00:33:08.653 --> 00:33:11.053
have you deliberately
poisoned this man?

00:33:11.122 --> 00:33:13.147
Relax.
He's just having gas pains.

00:33:13.224 --> 00:33:16.125
Your actions are not only
against regulations...

00:33:16.194 --> 00:33:18.788
Didn't I hear someone
threaten a mind-meld?

00:33:18.863 --> 00:33:20.228
I was merely trying

00:33:20.298 --> 00:33:23.233
to encourage the suspect
to be more forthcoming.

00:33:23.301 --> 00:33:24.393
Yeah.

00:33:24.469 --> 00:33:28.565
I think he's getting
all the encouragement he needs.

00:33:31.709 --> 00:33:33.404
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:33:33.478 --> 00:33:34.502
What is it?

00:33:34.579 --> 00:33:36.547
I need to prepare this patient
for discharge.

00:33:36.614 --> 00:33:37.911
I'm not finished with him yet.

00:33:37.982 --> 00:33:39.210
But Chellick's orders are to...

00:33:39.283 --> 00:33:41.649
Are to discharge the patient
at the end of the shift.

00:33:41.719 --> 00:33:42.845
The shift isn't over, is it?

00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:45.150
No, sir, but I need time
in order to get the patient...

00:33:45.223 --> 00:33:46.451
I'll tell you when he's ready.

00:33:46.524 --> 00:33:51.188
Dr. Voje, report to Level Blue
to assist Dr. Dysek in surgery.

00:34:04.075 --> 00:34:06.043
Voje!

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:11.744
I didn't realize
that any of this even existed.

00:34:11.816 --> 00:34:12.874
I need to talk to you.

00:34:12.950 --> 00:34:13.882
I don't have time.

00:34:13.951 --> 00:34:15.782
I just got a message
from the Allocator

00:34:15.853 --> 00:34:16.785
that Dysek needs me.

00:34:16.854 --> 00:34:18.185
I'm the one who sent for you.

00:34:18.256 --> 00:34:19.416
I used his access codes.

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:20.514
Oh.

00:34:20.591 --> 00:34:22.252
I need you to smuggle
my mobile emitter

00:34:22.326 --> 00:34:23.258
off Level Blue.

00:34:23.327 --> 00:34:27.354
Time has expired
for treatment of patient B-1.

00:34:27.432 --> 00:34:29.457
Proceed to patient B-3.

00:34:32.503 --> 00:34:35.438
The Medical Hologram
has one minute

00:34:35.506 --> 00:34:36.905
to treat patient B-3.

00:34:36.974 --> 00:34:37.941
You have to help me.

00:34:38.009 --> 00:34:39.203
12 patients on Level Red

00:34:39.277 --> 00:34:41.074
are being sent home
because of you.

00:34:41.145 --> 00:34:42.476
That's why we have to hurry.

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:44.242
We may still be able
to save them.

00:34:44.315 --> 00:34:46.146
You've already
endangered my patients,

00:34:46.217 --> 00:34:48.515
and now you're asking me
to risk my career?

00:34:48.586 --> 00:34:49.917
Why should I help you?

00:34:49.987 --> 00:34:52.922
Because I have a plan
to heal those patients.

00:34:52.990 --> 00:34:55.151
That's what doctors do...
we heal.

00:34:55.226 --> 00:34:57.490
So, choose... what kind of doctor
are you going to be?

00:34:57.562 --> 00:35:00.258
The Medical Hologram
has 30 seconds to deactivation.

00:35:00.331 --> 00:35:02.094
You hear that?

00:35:05.269 --> 00:35:06.896
How can I get you
off this level?

00:35:07.004 --> 00:35:09.234
Deactivate my mobile emitter,

00:35:09.307 --> 00:35:11.104
and put it in inside
this selenide medkit.

00:35:11.175 --> 00:35:12.301
It'll shield the signature.

00:35:12.376 --> 00:35:13.365
And then what?

00:35:13.444 --> 00:35:15.309
Take it to Level Red,
and reactivate me.

00:35:15.379 --> 00:35:18.212
What are you going to do
once you get to Level Red?

00:35:18.282 --> 00:35:21.274
The Medical Hologram has
ten seconds to deactivation.

00:35:21.352 --> 00:35:22.580
There's no time to explain.

00:35:22.653 --> 00:35:23.847
You'll have to trust me.

00:35:43.508 --> 00:35:46.500
I suspect young Dr.
Voje helped you escape.

00:35:46.577 --> 00:35:48.568
He had nothing to do with it.

00:35:48.646 --> 00:35:49.908
No matter.

00:35:49.981 --> 00:35:51.881
You're becoming
far too troublesome.

00:35:51.949 --> 00:35:54.417
I'm going to have to deactivate
your program.

00:35:55.987 --> 00:35:57.181
Voje!

00:35:58.756 --> 00:35:59.950
What's wrong with him?

00:36:00.024 --> 00:36:01.082
What are you doing?

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:02.854
A little experiment in empathy.

00:36:04.328 --> 00:36:05.761
You told me you
were just developing

00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:06.797
new treatment protocols.

00:36:06.864 --> 00:36:08.354
A single protocol, actually.

00:36:08.432 --> 00:36:10.900
You're only making things worse
for yourself.

00:36:11.002 --> 00:36:13.197
As a matter of fact,
I'm making things worse for you.

00:36:13.271 --> 00:36:15.501
I'm going to make you a patient
in your own hospital.

00:36:19.410 --> 00:36:20.707
What was in that injector?

00:36:20.778 --> 00:36:22.439
A neural blocker.

00:36:22.513 --> 00:36:25.414
Combined with the same virus
that afflicted Tebbis.

00:36:25.483 --> 00:36:26.814
I trusted you.

00:36:26.884 --> 00:36:28.010
And Tebbis trusted me.

00:36:28.085 --> 00:36:29.746
You remember Tebbis, don't you?

00:36:29.820 --> 00:36:31.685
Patient R-12?

00:36:31.756 --> 00:36:34.919
Maybe this will jog your memory.

00:36:35.059 --> 00:36:36.549
What are you doing?

00:36:36.627 --> 00:36:38.424
Patient R-12.

00:36:38.496 --> 00:36:41.158
Species: Dinaal.
Identity: Tebbis.

00:36:41.232 --> 00:36:43.928
This is ridiculous!
I'm not Tebbis!

00:36:44.035 --> 00:36:45.696
But the Allocator
thinks you are.

00:36:45.770 --> 00:36:46.862
How did you do?

00:36:46.938 --> 00:36:49.099
Simple... the Allocator
identifies patients

00:36:49.173 --> 00:36:50.470
by reading blood factors.

00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:52.509
I altered Chellick's
by injecting him

00:36:52.577 --> 00:36:54.238
with antigens from Tebbis.

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:58.180
Now, why don't we see if we can
get your condition treated.

00:36:58.249 --> 00:36:59.716
Requesting
one cytoglobin injection

00:36:59.784 --> 00:37:00.773
for patient R-12.

00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:03.820
Treatment denied.

00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:06.356
I order you to medicate me now.

00:37:06.424 --> 00:37:09.359
Ordinarily, I would,

00:37:09.427 --> 00:37:12.294
but if the Allocator says
"No"...

00:37:12.363 --> 00:37:14.297
Is this some sort of revenge?

00:37:14.365 --> 00:37:15.662
Not revenge.

00:37:15.733 --> 00:37:17.360
Leverage.

00:37:17.435 --> 00:37:19.027
I want enough cytoglobin

00:37:19.103 --> 00:37:21.003
to cure every infected patient
on this level.

00:37:21.072 --> 00:37:23.666
We don't have
an adequate supply.

00:37:23.741 --> 00:37:25.834
There's plenty on Level Blue.

00:37:25.910 --> 00:37:28.674
Where it's being used
to prevent arterial aging.

00:37:28.746 --> 00:37:30.475
Those patients
will survive without it,

00:37:30.548 --> 00:37:32.345
but a dozen people
on this level won't.

00:37:32.416 --> 00:37:34.407
I will not let them die.

00:37:41.325 --> 00:37:42.257
Entering orbit.

00:37:42.326 --> 00:37:43.588
Scan for the Doctor's signature.

00:37:50.434 --> 00:37:52.129
He's dying.

00:37:52.203 --> 00:37:53.534
As soon as we get
the cytoglobin,

00:37:53.604 --> 00:37:55.572
we'll be able to treat
all the Level Red patients,

00:37:55.640 --> 00:37:56.766
including him.

00:37:56.841 --> 00:37:59.207
You said it yourself...
doctors heal.

00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:01.142
We don't make patients sick!

00:38:01.212 --> 00:38:03.476
I don't know any other way
to help these people.

00:38:03.547 --> 00:38:05.515
Dr. Voje...

00:38:07.785 --> 00:38:10.345
I need the medicine now.

00:38:10.421 --> 00:38:13.720
Sir, I only have
a Level Red clearance.

00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:15.452
You know I'm not authorized.

00:38:15.526 --> 00:38:18.586
Then find someone who is.

00:38:26.337 --> 00:38:28.271
I've got him.

00:38:28.339 --> 00:38:30.899
He's aboard a vessel
above the northern continent.

00:38:30.975 --> 00:38:32.875
Can you get a lock?

00:38:32.943 --> 00:38:34.342
It's not going to be easy.

00:38:34.412 --> 00:38:35.845
His program
seems to be interfaced

00:38:35.913 --> 00:38:37.141
with the main computer.

00:38:37.214 --> 00:38:39.648
Hail the ship.

00:38:39.717 --> 00:38:42.709
They're responding;
audio only.

00:38:42.787 --> 00:38:44.687
This is Hospital Ship 42.

00:38:44.755 --> 00:38:47.053
Allocation Module Alpha.

00:38:47.124 --> 00:38:49.854
This is Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:38:49.927 --> 00:38:51.827
I would like
to speak with someone

00:38:51.896 --> 00:38:55.093
regarding a member of my crew
who is aboard your vessel.

00:38:55.166 --> 00:38:57.600
Administrator Chellick
is currently unavailable.

00:38:57.668 --> 00:38:59.932
Then may I speak
with someone else?

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:01.938
Only Administrator Chellick

00:39:02.006 --> 00:39:05.669
is authorized to communicate
with alien species.

00:39:13.417 --> 00:39:15.044
Are we having a problem here?

00:39:15.119 --> 00:39:17.644
Dysek. Finally.

00:39:17.722 --> 00:39:20.623
I-I'm sorry.
I had to tell him.

00:39:20.691 --> 00:39:23.182
What are you waiting for?

00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:24.522
Give me the cytoglobin.

00:39:24.595 --> 00:39:26.153
I don't think I can.

00:39:26.230 --> 00:39:27.697
What are you saying?

00:39:27.765 --> 00:39:30.393
Cytoglobin isn't authorized
for Level Red patients.

00:39:30.468 --> 00:39:31.196
Dysek!

00:39:31.268 --> 00:39:32.895
I don't want to break the rules.

00:39:32.970 --> 00:39:34.335
I made the rules!

00:39:34.405 --> 00:39:35.804
Then you should be pleased

00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:37.670
I hold them in such high regard.

00:39:37.742 --> 00:39:39.642
I'm sorry, Captain...
I can't transport him

00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:40.904
without damaging his matrix.

00:39:41.045 --> 00:39:42.842
Then you'll have
to go down there and get him.

00:39:42.913 --> 00:39:43.902
Aye, Captain.

00:39:44.048 --> 00:39:45.481
Chakotay.

00:39:50.287 --> 00:39:54.155
Don't tell me you're allied
with this defective hologram.

00:39:54.225 --> 00:39:57.683
No, but he has given me insight

00:39:57.762 --> 00:40:00.890
into some of the intricacies
of our system.

00:40:00.965 --> 00:40:02.899
For example, did you know

00:40:02.967 --> 00:40:05.561
if I don't request
enough resources

00:40:05.636 --> 00:40:07.570
for Level Blue this month,

00:40:07.638 --> 00:40:09.936
I won't get what I need
next month?

00:40:10.074 --> 00:40:11.905
What are you talking about?!

00:40:11.976 --> 00:40:13.944
You know, Doctor,
one way to increase

00:40:14.044 --> 00:40:16.376
your allocation of resources
on Level Blue

00:40:16.447 --> 00:40:19.416
would be to increase
the number of patients.

00:40:19.483 --> 00:40:21.474
I know at least a dozen people

00:40:21.552 --> 00:40:24.350
who should be treated
for arterial aging.

00:40:24.422 --> 00:40:28.222
Saving their lives would
be just a side effect.

00:40:28.292 --> 00:40:29.224
Hmm. Perhaps we should

00:40:29.293 --> 00:40:30.783
have them transferred
to Level Blue.

00:40:30.861 --> 00:40:33.056
If you're looking
for a second opinion, I concur.

00:40:33.130 --> 00:40:36.224
Well... Chellick...
what do you think?

00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:37.494
It's absurd!

00:40:37.568 --> 00:40:40.662
We'd have to transfer you
to Level Blue as well.

00:40:40.738 --> 00:40:42.797
You'd get your cytoglobin.

00:40:48.546 --> 00:40:49.911
Doctor.

00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:51.709
It's nice to see
some friendly faces.

00:40:51.782 --> 00:40:52.806
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:40:52.883 --> 00:40:53.815
Who do we talk to

00:40:53.884 --> 00:40:55.249
about accessing
their main computer?

00:40:55.319 --> 00:40:57.116
I'll be with you in a moment.

00:40:57.188 --> 00:40:59.713
I'm with a... patient.

00:41:01.258 --> 00:41:03.055
Do we have an agreement?

00:41:05.029 --> 00:41:07.497
Yes.

00:41:14.104 --> 00:41:16.572
You've managed to stay
well while I was away.

00:41:16.640 --> 00:41:18.733
I'm giving you
a clean bill of health.

00:41:18.809 --> 00:41:21.107
You were only away four days.

00:41:21.178 --> 00:41:23.373
A lot can happen in four days...

00:41:23.447 --> 00:41:26.245
injuries, infections...
malfunctions.

00:41:26.317 --> 00:41:27.784
As you said, I'm fine.

00:41:27.852 --> 00:41:29.376
Thank you.

00:41:29.453 --> 00:41:31.353
I was wondering
if you'd mind doing me a favor?

00:41:31.422 --> 00:41:34.687
I'd like you
to give me a checkup.

00:41:36.827 --> 00:41:39.295
Have you been
experiencing problems?

00:41:39.363 --> 00:41:41.888
No, but as you said,

00:41:41.966 --> 00:41:44.332
I've been off the ship
for awhile,

00:41:44.401 --> 00:41:47.632
interfaced
with an alien computer.

00:41:49.573 --> 00:41:51.063
Your program appears
to be operating

00:41:51.141 --> 00:41:52.768
within normal parameters.

00:41:52.843 --> 00:41:54.674
Really?

00:41:54.745 --> 00:41:57.145
What about over
the past several days?

00:41:58.949 --> 00:42:02.646
There's no indication
of diminished capacity.

00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:05.780
No problems
with my ethical subroutines?

00:42:07.725 --> 00:42:09.317
None.

00:42:09.393 --> 00:42:11.224
I see.

00:42:11.295 --> 00:42:13.627
You seem disappointed.

00:42:19.136 --> 00:42:21.468
While I was aboard that ship...

00:42:21.539 --> 00:42:23.473
I poisoned a man.

00:42:23.541 --> 00:42:24.508
Deliberately?

00:42:24.575 --> 00:42:25.735
Yes.

00:42:25.809 --> 00:42:27.470
I was trying to force him

00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:29.274
to let me treat patients
who were dying.

00:42:31.582 --> 00:42:33.516
You were prepared
to sacrifice an individual

00:42:33.584 --> 00:42:35.347
to benefit a collective.

00:42:35.419 --> 00:42:37.353
No offense, Seven,

00:42:37.421 --> 00:42:40.447
but I don't exactly aspire
to Borg ideals.

00:42:43.928 --> 00:42:47.125
You were hoping your behavior
was the result of a malfunction.

00:42:50.868 --> 00:42:52.358
I'm sorry, Doctor,

00:42:52.436 --> 00:42:55.701
but I must give you
a clean bill of health.
